Personally, I dislike the character classes that start with random
items.  It's a crock and leads to some silly game strategies that
favor people with enormous patience.  There's enough of that in 
Hack already.

My feeling is that starting characters should either (a) start with
set items and set statistics (like Rogue) thus eliminating luck and
restarting at the beginning of the game or (b) have user-defined
characteristics, by allowing the player to allocate characteristic
points and buy starting equipment.

I like (b) better myself.
